<P>In the booklet&nbsp;<STRONG>Neil Tennant</STRONG> talks about the <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> reference in their single <STRONG>"DJ Culture"</STRONG>: <BR><BR><FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #ffff00">"There were a lot of bs attitudes going on in the early Nineties, and the song is about how facile and pretentious modern life was. The 3rd verse is about how, if you have no history, you can reinvent yourself. There’s a reference to <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> in it - "She after Sean"; after her marriage with <STRONG>Sean Penn</STRONG> broke up she sort of came back as a sex goddess."</FONT> <BR><BR>Also in their video for "DJ culture" there’s a Madonna look a like in the <STRONG>"Open your Heart"</STRONG> look! (Beginning at around 3.10).</P><img src="/corrispondenti/co-martin.jpg" border="0">
