    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>Portuguese national TV station <STRONG>RTP 1</STRONG>&nbsp;will broadcast the <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> concert.</P>
<P>They’re currently broadcasting a few adverts including some footage of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> (from&nbsp;the <STRONG>Confessions Tour DVD</STRONG> and from the <STRONG>Live 8</STRONG> concert). <STRONG><FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #ffff00">"Hey You" is the official song for every adverts for the show</FONT></STRONG>. </P>
<P>The same day of the <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> concert - July 7th -&nbsp;there will be also a great concert with the greatest Portuguese artists at the Atlantic Pavillion in Lisbon, where <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> performed during the European leg of the <STRONG>re-Invention Tour</STRONG> and also where she opened the <STRONG>Europe Music Awards</STRONG> show in 2005. </P>
<P>For more information visit: <A href="http://www.rtp.pt" target=_blank>www.rtp.pt</A>.&nbsp;&nbsp;<BR><BR>Special thanks to <STRONG>David Guedes</STRONG> and <STRONG>Sara</STRONG>.</P>
<P align=center><IMG src="/images/2007/more.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=justify>In <STRONG>New Zealand</STRONG> the <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> will&nbsp;be broadcast&nbsp;on <STRONG>C4</STRONG> at 8pm 7th of July.</P>
<P align=justify>Furthermore, the Eastern Bay Of Plenty’s local radio station <STRONG>1XX</STRONG> has secured exclusive rights to broadcast the best of <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG>. </P>
<P align=justify>Tune into <STRONG>Radio 1XX</STRONG> throughout the Eastern Bay Of Plenty on <STRONG>90.5FM</STRONG>, <STRONG>1242AM</STRONG> and <STRONG>93.0FM</STRONG> at Ohope Beach or through the station’s website <A href="http://www.1xx.co.nz" target=_blank>www.1xx.co.nz</A>. <STRONG>1XX</STRONG>’s broadcast of the <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> concerts will also be simulcast through <STRONG>92.9 Kiwi FM</STRONG> in Te Puke. <BR><BR>The <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> broadcast on <STRONG>Radio 1XX</STRONG> begins at 10:30am on Sunday 8th July.<BR><BR>Special thanks to our correspondent <STRONG>Henrique Ricky</STRONG>.</P>
<P align=justify><EM>Send all your info to </EM><A href="mailto:dm@drownedmadonna.com"><EM>dm@drownedmadonna.com</EM></A><EM>. And do NOT forget that you can have the chance to have your <STRONG>photos</STRONG> and <STRONG>stories</STRONG> from the <STRONG>Live Earth</STRONG> published on the next issue of the <STRONG>DM Fanzine</STRONG>!</EM></P>
</font></div>
